Z||000000||TTiger||12-19-2001||01:56 PM||||This one might be best for the ladies on the forum, but guys, any opinions are definately welcome!!<P>I have just started dating a girl within the last month.  Last night I asked her what she wanted for Christmas, and she told me that she has everything that she needs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> This just makes me mad.  Now I have no clue what to get her, not even the faintest idea.<P>Any ideas??  Keep in mind that I am a poor college student  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Tony<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttigersig_13.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||thomas_l||12-19-2001||02:03 PM||||Breakfast in bed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||12-19-2001||02:16 PM||||Depends on what type of woman she is... <P>If she likes romantics, then be creative.  Hand-make a set of coupons only for her with items like: condlelight dinner for 2 (prepared by you), massage (by you, of course), a hug & kiss (always good), stay home for a night (not with "the guys" or "the forum"), etc. (even non-romantic women tend to like this stuff).<P>If she's not romantic, then something nice and simple.  Does she collect anything?  Is there anything that really fits her personality? Is she athletic?  Does she have a favorite clothing store? (I know Gift Certificates suck, but if worse comes to worse).<P>Since you've only been dating a short amount of time, keep the cost down. No jewelery, no furs, etc.<P>Maybe if you tell us something about her, we could be more helpful!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||TTiger||12-19-2001||02:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>Depends on what type of woman she is... <P>If she likes romantics, then be creative.  Hand-make a set of coupons only for her with items like: condlelight dinner for 2 (prepared by you), massage (by you, of course), a hug & kiss (always good), stay home for a night (not with "the guys" or "the forum"), etc. (even non-romantic women tend to like this stuff).<P>If she's not romantic, then something nice and simple.  Does she collect anything?  Is there anything that really fits her personality? Is she athletic?  Does she have a favorite clothing store? (I know Gift Certificates suck, but if worse comes to worse).<P>Since you've only been dating a short amount of time, keep the cost down. No jewelery, no furs, etc.<P>Maybe if you tell us something about her, we could be more helpful!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree, I will not get too expensive yet.  She actually made a comment on that a few weeks ago about one of my friends.  I like the coupon idea, though.  I will definately consider that one.<P>She is very into fitness.  I don't think she collects much of anything, though, and she shops just about everywhere (typical  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>I have to go to work now.  Keep the ideas coming!<BR>Tony<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttigersig_14.gif"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||JSocha||12-19-2001||02:23 PM||||Stuffed fuzzy little animal (Teddy Bear, Christmas Bear, Rabbit, etc.) and a rose (Fire and Ice Rose). <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||12
Z||000005||AusFiero||12-19-2001||03:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>Depends on what type of woman she is... <P>If she likes romantics, then be creative.  Hand-make a set of coupons only for her with items like: condlelight dinner for 2 (prepared by you), massage (by you, of course), a hug & kiss (always good), stay home for a night (not with "the guys" or "the forum"), etc. (even non-romantic women tend to like this stuff).<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hehehe Minn. How to give a present without spending. You cheapskate you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> J/K<P><P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/auschristmas.gif">        <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000006||Jaygee79||12-19-2001||03:04 PM||||i like the idea of a christmas teddy bear.  and get a single rose and make the bear holding it.  that would be cute.||||reg||1
