Z||000013||JSocha||12-19-2001||06:57 PM||||I couldn't believe it when my wife told me all she wanted was the perfect lump of coal.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  As you can imagine, I was a happy little camper.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> Then she added that the coal had to have been under extreme pressure for many, many, if not millions of years prior to this Christmas when she is to receive it as her gift.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  Women!  Always with the stipulations. &lt;*sigh*&gt;||||reg||11
Z||000014||annieL||12-19-2001||08:10 PM||||If you have a Bath and Body Works around you which i'm sure you do get her something from there. Plumeria, Sugar Plum, Juniper Breeze and Cucumber Melon are very nice scents and you can get lotion, spray, and bath gel at a really good price. <P>Good Luck!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000015||fierobaby||12-19-2001||08:27 PM||||here's my thought... a blanket like a really soft one... that way when you're not around she can stay warm.... I also like the stuffed animal idea... I actually asked for sweatshirt for christmas but I dunno if thats what I'm getting... I would be happy with just about anything minus doggy poop! Hey wait get her a PIE PET! its like cow poop with boggly eyes on it! J/K||||reg||1
Z||000016||TTiger||12-20-2001||12:32 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>maybe shes testing you - to see how well you 'know her'<P>ie. "If I have to tell you what to get me for christmas then it wont mean anything if you buy it for me..."</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That would really suck because I don't know her all that well.  That's the problem.  I just started seeing her like 4 weeks ago!!<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaygee79:<BR><B> we just say that because we don't want to sound like greedy little snots.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't think that's what she meant, but possibly.  I know that she is a very materialistic girl  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierobaby:<BR><B>I would be happy with just about anything minus doggy poop! Hey wait get her a PIE PET! its like cow poop with boggly eyes on it! J/K</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>HEY, where can I get one of those boggly eye cow poop things???  She has that kind of a sense of humor, and I know she would laugh!!<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>Lets ask the ladies on the forum what they think of the "Fire and Ice" rose and if they would love to receive one:</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Where can I get one of those roses?? That is very nice.  <P>I am almost partial to the coupon idea right now, but that is not enough.  I don't want to seem that cheap  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  She also has like the entire Bath and Body Works store in her bathroom right now (always smells great  <IMG SRC="http://www.theunholytrinity.org/cracks_smileys/contrib/splarka/as-drool.gif">  )<P>I like the ideas so far, keep them coming!!<BR>Tony<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttigersig_15.gif"> <P>||||reg||1
